{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Built and queued the probe that answers the parent configuration question's remaining open discriminator — the installed-snapshot repair path. A node is snapshotted before a configuration change, taken down while the cluster commits eighty further entries (letting the leader snapshot and compact its log past that node's next index), then restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs; the run records the recovered configuration, the node's snapshot index and the leader's, waits for the configuration in force to be restored, and records whether the node's snapshot index jumped, which distinguishes an installed snapshot from log replication. Locally the node regained the full configuration and its snapshot index moved from 11 to 98, so the repair arrived with an installed snapshot; the retained receipt is unread and no account for it has been recorded yet.\"}"}}
